# BK-0011M BOS ROM, 140000-157777. System-call names come from common.ann.
# Section comments are from reading the code, checked against the BOS
# manual 00015-01.32.01 where it says something about the same thing.

code 140000 RESET ; power-on entry: the VM1 starts at SEL1's high byte, 140000
head 140000 Power-on: mask interrupts and go to the cold start.

ptrs 140010 134
head 140010 System call table (BOS manual §2.3): one slot per EMT 0-133.
head 140010 JSR PC,@slot calls a routine directly; EMT n goes through EMTDSP.

code 140300 COLD
head 140300 Cold start. Stack at 1000; system RAM page 7 at 040000 and ROM
head 140300 page 1 at 100000; set up low memory (INIVEC); print the banner
head 140300 (BANNER, in ROM page 1) and scroll it up the screen.
note 140370 user mapping copy: 040000 = RAM page 5 (screen 0), 100000 = RAM page 4
note 140376 key held down at power-on?
note 140404 yes: skip booting, go to the monitor
note 140406 floppy controller found?
note 140414 .BABOOT: boot from floppy
head 140420 Scan ROM pages 3, 2, 1, 0 (R0 = 413 down to 410). For each page that
head 140420 exists, call 120000 if it answers, then 100000 if it answers. Page 1
head 140420 is only called if it starts with NOP (000240), the autostart marker
head 140420 that BASIC page 1 carries. Vector 4 catches missing ROMs meanwhile.

code 140562 MONENT
head 140562 Enter the keyboard monitor.

code 140576 TRAP4 ; default handler for vector 4 and all unused vectors
head 140576 Catch-all trap handler (INIVEC points vectors 4-376 here). SEL1
head 140576 bit 2 is set by HALT and the STOP key but not by a bus error
head 140576 (BOS manual §1.3): HALT/STOP go to the monitor, a bus error goes
head 140576 to the user's .BTRPS handler if one is set. Leaves with RTT.
note 140602 save SEL1: bit 2 = HALT or STOP rather than a bus error

code 140712 MONITR
head 140712 Keyboard monitor: take over vector 4, save the interrupted PC and
head 140712 PSW, then continue in ROM page 1 at 120002 (MONMAI).

code 150170 INIVEC
head 150170 Set up low memory: JMP @#BEXIT at address 0, so a jump to 0 returns
head 150170 to the monitor; every vector 4-376 -> TRAP4 at PSW 2341. Vectors 100
head 150170 and 274 point at their own PSW word, which holds 000002 (RTI), so
head 150170 they return at once until a driver installs a real handler.
note 150176 address 0: JMP @#BEXIT
note 150232 vector 100 -> 102, which holds RTI
note 150254 vector 274 -> 276, which holds RTI

code 152112 EMTDSP
head 152112 EMT dispatcher. The low byte of the EMT instruction picks a slot in
head 152112 the system call table (EMT 0-133). The caller's C flag is passed in,
head 152112 and the routine's C flag passed back, through the saved PSW. Larger
head 152112 EMT numbers go to the user's handler in EMTUSR (166), or print an
head 152112 error and enter the monitor.
note 152132 caller's C flag -> C
note 152144 C -> saved PSW


# From gid's partial IDA disassembly of the BK-0011M system ROMs 324 and 325
# ("Попытка дизассемблирования ПЗУ БОС БК0011М", 324_diz.7z from
# https://gid.pdp-11.net/misc.html); its input's MD5 is that of
# b11m_ext.rom and b11m_bos.rom together, and 4112 of its instructions
# match these ROMs. Its names (long ones shortened to six characters, the
# source's given) and its comments, translated; where this file or
# bk0011m.ann already names an address, from the BOS manual, that name stays.

code 140502 TT4T1

code 140550 TT4T2

code 140772 TT4T3

code 141042 CM$G$
head 141042 Monitor command "G": run a program from the address given.

code 141072 CM$P$
head 141072 Monitor command "P": go on with the program from where it was stopped.

code 141216 CM$STP
head 141216 Monitor command ШАГ: run one instruction of the program and come back to
head 141216 the monitor.

code 141246 CM$C$
head 141246 Monitor command "C": map the page given into the window given.

code 141650 OUT8WB
head 141650 Print an octal number. In: R0 = the number; C clear for a word, set for
head 141650 a byte.

code 141750 CM$L$
head 141750 Monitor command "L": load from tape.

code 142602 TT4T4

code 142722 WRUSRW
head 142722 Write a word in the user's address space. In: R5 = address, R0 = the
head 142722 word. (WRITEWORDUSER in the source.)

code 142746 WRUSRB
head 142746 Write a byte in the user's address space. In: R5 = address, R0 = the
head 142746 byte. (WRITEBYTEUSER.)

code 142772 RDUSRW
head 142772 Read a word from the user's address space. In: R5 = address. Out: R0.
head 142772 (READWORDUSER.)

code 143016 RDUSRB
head 143016 Read a byte from the user's address space. In: R5 = address. Out: R0.
head 143016 (READBYTEUSER.)

code 143644 BEEP
head 143644 A beep.

code 143654 SOUND

code 143712 CLRSCR
head 143712 Fill the screen with the background color.

code 146446 CURSOR

code 146530 OCUW64
head 146530 Draw the cursor in 64-character mode.

code 146552 OCUW80

code 146634 OCUW32
head 146634 Draw the cursor in 32-character or double-width mode.

code 147114 MONV60
head 147114 Keyboard interrupt (vector 60).

code 147124 MONV274
head 147124 Keyboard interrupt with АР2 (vector 274).

code 147304 KBBEEP
head 147304 The key click.

code 147650 CKBRST
head 147650 Initialize the keyboard buffer.

code 150354 TT4ROT

code 151576 TT4EDS

code 154544 MOTOFF
head 154544 Stop the tape motor. (MOTOROFF$ in the source.)

code 154554 MOTCTL
head 154554 Tape motor: R0 = 0 off, otherwise on. (MOTORCTRL$.)

name 154752 B10OPT
head 154752 The BK-0010 tape format's operations. (B10OPTBL.)

code 154762 TT4B10

code 155076 CHKSUM
head 155076 Checksum. In: R1 = array, R2 = its length in bytes. Out: R0 = the sum.
head 155076 (CALCCHKSUM.)

code 155134 MOTON
head 155134 Start the tape motor. (MOTORON$.)

code 155150 B10CM0
head 155150 Write a file.

code 155316 OUTSYN
head 155316 Write the pilot and the sync pulse. In: R0 = length, R4 and R5 = the
head 155316 half-periods. (OUTSYNCRO$.)

code 155406 SAVBLK
head 155406 Write a block of data after a buffer sequence. In: R1 = block, R2 =
head 155406 length. (SAVEBLOCK$.)

code 155424 SAVBL1
head 155424 Write a block of data. In: R1 = block, R2 = length. (SAVEBLK1$.)

code 155432 OUTBYT
head 155432 Write a byte. (OUTBYTE$.)

code 155464 OUTBT1
head 155464 Write a 1 bit (+1, -1). (OUTBIT1$.)

code 155546 B10CM3

code 155554 B10CM2

code 155560 B10CM1
head 155560 Read a file.

code 155662 FNDFIL
head 155662 Find the start of a file. (FINDFILEBEGIN$.)

code 156042 RDHEAD
head 156042 Read a file's header and compare its name. Out: C if the name differs.
head 156042 (READHEADER$.)

code 156126 RDFILE
head 156126 Read a file. (READFILE$.)

code 156254 GETADR
head 156254 The file's load address into R1. (GETREADADDR$.)

code 156270 RDBLK
head 156270 Read a block after its buffer sequence. In: R1 = address, R2 = length in
head 156270 bytes. (READBLOCK$.)

code 156350 RDBLK1
head 156350 Read a block. In: R1 = address, R2 = length in bytes. (READBLK1$.)

code 156420 PULSE
head 156420 Measure a pulse: its length into R4. (CALCPULSE$.)

code 156504 B10PGS
head 156504 Set up the pages for the BK-0010 tape format. (SETB10PAGES$.)

name 157346 KBMPRM
head 157346 The keyboard monitor's prompt.

name 157506 ROMPGM

name 157513 MPGMW0

name 157523 MPGMW1

name 157533 ILLJMR

name 157574 ILLEMT

name 157672 CMDSUB
head 157672 Monitor command ШАГ (step).
